quizQuestions=[]
def quiz(id,module,prompt,choices,correct,explanation):
    quizQuestions.append(dict(id=id,moduleId=module,prompt=prompt,choices=choices,correctIndex=correct,explanation=explanation))
quiz('q-benchmark','benchmark-hygiene','Which evidence best supports a performance improvement claim?',['One fastest run after editing the code','Correctness checks, a controlled baseline, repeated measurements and recorded configuration','A profiler screenshot without the input or hardware details','A larger input for only the optimized version'],1,'Correctness, controlled inputs, repeated timing and a recorded environment make the comparison interpretable and reproducible. A single best run hides variance.')
quiz('q-locality','cache-locality','Why might sequential traversal outperform random traversal of the same array?',['Sequential order guarantees every access hits L1','Random traversal always uses more arithmetic','Sequential access can improve locality and let prefetching anticipate future accesses','The compiler must remove all sequential loads'],2,'Sequential access often uses nearby elements in each fetched cache line and gives hardware prefetchers a predictable pattern. The actual result still depends on working-set size and hardware.')
quiz('q-raii','cpp-lifetime','What is the central idea of RAII?',['Tie resource ownership to object lifetime so destruction releases the resource','Move every object to avoid allocation','Use global variables for every resource','Manually release resources after every expression'],0,'RAII connects resource acquisition and release to object construction and destruction. It helps maintain correct cleanup across normal control flow and exceptions.')
quiz('q-tail','engine-optimization','Why report p95/p99 as well as throughput?',['Percentiles eliminate all measurement noise','Throughput alone proves every request is fast','Tail percentiles measure source-code complexity','Aggregate throughput can hide slow requests in the latency distribution'],3,'Throughput measures work completed per time interval. Tail-latency percentiles describe the slower requests, which can matter even when aggregate throughput looks good.')
quiz('q-cuda','cuda-memory','Which adjacent-thread access pattern is generally favorable for coalescing?',['Each thread accesses an unrelated allocation','Adjacent threads access adjacent suitably aligned elements','Every thread serially reads the full input','Every warp uses a different numerical precision'],1,'Nearby addresses requested by neighboring threads can be served efficiently by memory transactions. Alignment and the precise access pattern matter; measure the real kernel.')
quiz('q-pipeline','fixed-point-mac','A pipeline has latency 5 cycles and initiation interval 1. What does that imply?',['Every result takes only 1 cycle from input','Only one input may enter every 5 cycles','It can accept a new input each cycle, with each result emerging 5 cycles later','Its clock frequency is exactly 5 GHz'],2,'Latency is the input-to-output delay; initiation interval is the spacing between accepted inputs. They are different quantities, and neither alone determines clock frequency.')
quiz('q-dma','axi-dma','What is needed for a fair FPGA latency report?',['Report core compute and data-transfer/end-to-end timing separately','Report only the HLS estimated cycle count as host latency','Exclude all numerical checks','Assume DMA has zero overhead'],0,'The arithmetic pipeline and the ARM/host/DMA path have different timing boundaries. Reporting both shows whether data movement dominates the actual application.')
quiz('q-int8','quantization','After quantizing a model to INT8, what should be checked?',['Only that the output tensor exists','Only that the model file is smaller','Training accuracy on the same data used to tune quantization','Held-out accuracy, numerical conventions, resource use and measured performance'],3,'Lower precision changes numerical behavior as well as storage and compute costs. Evaluate on a held-out set, document scales/zero points or fixed-point conventions, and measure the actual target.')
measurementRules=['Establish correctness against a reference before optimizing.','Pin input sizes, seeds, model versions, precision, compiler flags and hardware.','Separate setup, transfer, compute and end-to-end response time.','Warm up appropriately; repeat measurements and report distribution/variance.','Use fair optimized CPU and relevant GPU-library baselines.','Separate FPGA pipeline latency from ARM/host/DMA overhead.','Report numerical accuracy and resource/energy methodology when changing precision.','Retain failed or regressing experiments with explanations.','Store scripts and raw benchmark data with charts.']
